1. systemd vs init ls -l /sbin/init
2. systemctl get-default  ( graghical, muti-user,etc )
3. systemctl set-default <target> 
4. lshw => get all details about all hardware connected to the server
5. sudo -i => to switch to the root user
6. file <filename> => details about file type


1. users types ( User Account, System Account, Super user)
2. id <username> => get details about a specfic user
3. useradd -d <homedir> -s <shell> -g <main group> -G <groups> -p <username> 
4. usermod -d <homedir> -s <shell> -g <main group> -G <groups> <username>
5. userdel <username> => to delete a user
6. passwd <username> => to set or udpate password of a user
7. su -c <command> <username> => to run a command as a different user
8. /etc/passwd => contains details about users
9. /etc/group  => contans details about group
10. visudo => to edit the sudeors file /etc/sudoers
11. who => to see who are logging to the server
12. last => last activity in the server

